{
  "note": "What an impersonated token may reach (AC-1-g, ADR-0136, catalog §3.6). Hand-written and language-neutral, like wire.json (ADR-0036): auth-handler holds a copy for every gated router (impersonation.go) and auth-service for its own routes, which are not behind the gate (shared-core http/impersonation.ts); a test on each side pins the copy to this file. Anything not listed is refused 403 impersonation.blockedAction — a new route is closed until someone adds it here. `path` is the public path the browser asks for; a `:name` segment matches one segment. `tools/contracts.py` fails when an `allow` row names no route, or falls under `never`.",
